  "question": {
    "text": "One mole of an ideal gas is taken along the process in which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></math> = constant. The graph shown represents the variation of molar heat capacity of such a gas with respect to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>. The values of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>'</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>'</mo></math>. respectively, are given by<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0137_e709b8732d98.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 150px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>5</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mtext>R</mtext> <mtext>,&nbsp;</mtext> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>5</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>",
